<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>" dir="<%= SupportedLocales.dir(I18n.locale) %>">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
  </head>
  <%# Only the pages that are meant to be full-bleed lock the viewport: the
      player (and the owner's @chromeless preview of it), and the signed-in
      shell, which scrolls inside its own fixed container below. The
      unauthenticated auth pages — sign in, register, password reset, invite
      acceptance — are ordinary documents that can be taller than the viewport
      (register always is; any of them is once a phone keyboard is up), so they
      have to scroll like a normal page. `overflow:hidden` didn't stop them
      being scrolled, only the user: the browser still scrolls a focused field
      into view, so clicking into a text box moved the page and then stranded
      it there with no way to scroll back — and it put the legal footer
      permanently out of reach. %>
  <% viewport_locked = Current.user || @chromeless || controller_name == "player" %>
  <body style="<%= viewport_locked ? "height:100dvh;min-height:100vh;overflow:hidden;" : "min-height:100dvh;" %>background:#272D4A;color:#F7F7F7;font-family:'ABeeZee',sans-serif;">
    <%# @chromeless pages (e.g. the owner's Verto preview) render bare even
        when signed in, so they replicate exactly what a respondent sees. %>
    <% if Current.user && !@chromeless %>
      <div data-controller="command-palette">
        <%# @hide_main_nav pages (the editor) drop the top nav to free the
            space, but keep the command palette reachable via ⌘K. %>
        <%= render "shared/bottom_bar" unless @hide_main_nav %>
        <%= render "shared/command_palette" %>
      </div>
      <div style="position: fixed; top: <%= @hide_main_nav ? "0" : "56px" %>; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; overflow: auto;">
        <%= yield %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <%# Unauthenticated chrome-less pages (login, register, password). The
          player has its own content-language switcher in its nav. %>
      <%# The respondent account (@own_top_bar) draws a bar of its own with the
          switcher inside it, so the fixed corner would put a second one on
          top of the first. The legal footer below still renders there. %>
      <% unless controller_name == "player" || @chromeless || @own_top_bar %>
        <div class="lang-switcher-fixed"><%= render "shared/locale_switcher" %></div>
      <% end %>
      <%= yield %>
      <%# Same non-player, non-chromeless gate as the locale switcher above —
          the player's own consent gate is enough there; a second links footer
          would clutter its full-viewport experience. %>
      <% unless controller_name == "player" || @chromeless %>
        <%= render "shared/legal_footer" %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
